  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="order-title">One custom order, from advance to balance</h2>
      <p>Made-to-order work spreads a single sale across months. Each stage leaves its own record. This is our general analysis, so adjust it to how you work.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Stages of a custom order and their records, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Question to raise</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Advance taken</th><td>A receipt linked to an order number</td><td>Does the advance need any GST entry, and when is it income?</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Materials issued</th><td>Timber, ply, laminate and hardware against that order</td><td>How do we value part-finished work at year end?</td></tr>
